d Test Infrastructure table.\n71\tState B: Filesystem scan:\n72\t\n73\t```bash\n74\tfind . -name \"pytest.ini\" -o -name \"jest.config.*\" -o -name \"vitest.config.*\" -o -name \"pyproject.toml\" 2>/dev/null | head -10\n75\tfind . \\( -name \"*.test.*\" -o -name \"*.spec.*\" -o -name \"test_*\" \\) -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null | head -40\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\t### 2d. Cross-Reference\n79\t\n80\tMatch each requirement to existing tests by filename, imports, test descriptions. Record: requirement → test_file → status.\n81\t\n82\t## 3. Gap Analysis\n83\t\n84\tClassify each requirement:\n85\t\n86\t| Status | Criteria |\n87\t|--------|----------|\n88\t| COVERED | Test exists, targets behavior, runs green |\n89\t| PARTIAL | Test exists, failing or incomplete |\n90\t| MISSING | No test found |\n91\t\n92\tBuild: `{ task_id, requirement, gap_type, suggested_test_path, suggested_command }`\n93\t\n94\tNo gaps → skip to Step 6, set `nyquist_compliant: true`.\n95\t\n96\t## 4. Present Gap Plan\n97\t\n98\t**Text mode (`workflow.text_mode: true` in config or `--text` flag):** Set `TEXT_MODE=true` if `--text` is present in `$ARGUMENTS` OR `text_mode` from init JSON is `true`. When TEXT_MODE is active, replace every `AskUserQuestion` call with a plain-text numbered list and ask the user to type their choice number. This is required for non-Claude runtimes (OpenAI Codex, Antigravity, etc.) where `AskUserQuestion` is not available.\n99\tCall AskUserQuestion with gap table and options:\n100\t1. \"Fix all gaps\" → Step 5\n101\t2. \"Skip — mark manual-only\" → add to Manual-Only, Step 6\n102\t3. \"Cancel\" → exit\n103\t\n104\t## 5. Spawn gsd-nyquist-auditor\n105\t\n106\tPrint: `◆ Spawning nyquist auditor... (runs in a subagent — no output until it returns, ~1–5 min; expected, not a freeze)`\n107\t\n108\t<!-- #2508 runtime-aware-dispatch -->\n109\t\n110\t> **Runtime-aware dispatch (#2508 Phase 4).** GSD workflows dispatch specialized subagents by role. Before dispatching on a b